 "_doc": "Mix settings applied by tools/build_reaper.py. gain_db -> track volume; seat/width -> REAPER stereo pan mode (I_PANMODE 5, D_PAN, D_WIDTH); mics: Opus mic channels to load and their volumes (null = keep the patch's own); every other mic is unloaded; send: per-mic Reverb Send level; the Opus reverb on fx:0 of every patch is replaced by reverb.from_patch's at reverb.fx_volume. Opus sub-channel pans are set to 0. c02: dyn_trim_db {f, ff}: level trim in dB that is 0 at CC46 (p) and reaches f at CC88 and ff at CC114, read from the printed dynamic curve (dyn_curve), and soft_trim_db {ppp, pp} for every track except timpani; both go into the track volume envelope with parts.json vol_db, so CC11 keeps choosing the dynamic layer. c03: a track may carry its own soft_trim_db, which replaces the global one. c04: a track's eq is a ReaEQ after Opus (band lowshelf: ReaEQ band 1 low shelf; bell: band 2; unused bands at 0 dB and the high-pass band disabled), applied on rebuild and by --mix-only. c05: seat/width are written into Opus (every mic channel's panLeft = seat - width, panRight = seat + width; the reverb return fx:0 centred at full width) and the REAPER pan is centre/width 1 (C #3); the hall is EW's 'New Hollywood Hall 2.0' from 3BS Sus MAX (C #1); eq band 'highpass' enables ReaEQ band 4 as a high pass (C #2).",
